  "text": "Veterinary Oncology | Dog Oncology in Hattiesburg and Petal\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\nAbout\nOur Hospital\nWhy Trust Us?\nOur Vets\nOur Team\nLab\nCore Care\nVaccinations & Prevention\nWellness Exams\nDental Care\nInternal Medicine\nAcupuncture & Holistic Care\nCold Laser Therapy\nExotic Pets\nCancer Care\nPuppies & Kittens\nGeriatric Care\nSurgery\nSurgical Services\nSpaying & Neutering\nSoft Tissue Surgery\nOrthopedic Surgery\nC-Sections\nEmergencies\nPatients\nPatient Information\nFear Free Certified Vets\nFinancing Options\nPet Care Tips & Advice\nCareers\nShop\nContact\nSearch\nSearch\nFacebook\nGoogleBusiness\nSkip to Main Content\nAccessible Version\nStandard Version\nFacebook\nGoogleBusiness\n2010 Evelyn Gandy Pkwy\nHattiesburg\nMS\n39401\nUS\nBook Online\n(601) 544-3290\nAbout\nOur Hospital\nWhy Trust Us?\nOur Vets\nOur Team\nLab\nCore Care\nVaccinations & Prevention\nWellness Exams\nDental Care\nInternal Medicine\nAcupuncture & Holistic Care\nCold Laser Therapy\nExotic Pets\nCancer Care\nPuppies & Kittens\nGeriatric Care\nSurgery\nSurgical Services\nSpaying & Neutering\nSoft Tissue Surgery\nOrthopedic Surgery\nC-Sections\nEmergencies\nPatients\nPatient Information\nFear Free Certified Vets\nFinancing Options\nPet Care Tips & Advice\nCareers\nShop\nContact\nOpen Search Dialog\nLimited Time Offer\nEnjoy a $25 First Exam – Learn More\n×\nClose\nSearch\nSearch\nVeterinary Oncology\nAt The Pet Hospital (Parkway) in Hattiesburg, our veterinarians use diagnostics and treatments to provide the best possible care to pets with cancer.\nBook Online\n(601) 544-3290\nAdvanced Cancer Care for Hattiesburg Pets\nCancer is a disease that affects both humans and animals, and it can affect even the healthiest ones. The good news is that it can be treated with several advanced methods.\nAt The Pet Hospital (Parkway), our Hattiesburg vet oncologists are committed to providing care and\nemergency treatments\nfor pets with cancer, and support for the individuals and families that love them.\nAfter reviewing your pet’s medical history and\nlab diagnosis\nwe will sit down with you and your pet to discuss the disease, staging (additional diagnostics), treatment options, and prognosis.\nStaging & Diagnostics\nAfter a diagnosis of cancer, additional\ndiagnostic testing\ncan help to determine the extent of cancer in the body, which allows us to optimize treatment options and better predict prognosis.\nAt The Pet Hospital (Parkway), we offer in-house laboratory services and diagnostics to provide treatment for pets with cancer.\nTreatment Options\nWhen staging is complete, our oncology vets will discuss all the appropriate treatment options.\nCancer can be treated by several different therapies or combinations of treatments including\nsurgery\n, chemotherapy, radiation therapy, immunotherapy, targeted therapies, or\npalliative care\nwhen appropriate.\n« Go Back\nNew Patients Welcome\nThe Pet Hospital (Parkway) is accepting new patients! Our experienced vets are passionate about the health of companion animals in Hattiesburg and Petal. Get in touch today to book your pet's first appointment.\nContact Us\nThe Pet Hospital (Parkway)\nHome\nAbout\nCore Care\nSurgery\nEmergencies\nPatients\nCareers\nContact\nPrivacy Policy\nDo Not Sell or Share My Personal Information\nTerms & Conditions\nAccessibility\nSearch\nSitemap\nBack to Top\nFacebook\nGoogleBusiness\nCopyright © 2026. All Rights Reserved.\nPart of the\nPetVet Care Centers Network\n.\nPanther\nContact Panther Location\nParkway\nContact Parkway Location\nOpen Menu\nClose Menu\n×\nIMPORTANT NOTICE:\nDue to Hurricane Isaias, our hours and availability may be affected. Please call us before visiting to be we sure we are open and able to provide pet care at this time.\nCall\n(601) 544-3290\nOpen Modal",
